# config/subsys/Kconfig.ports: the ported programs (third_party/ports).
#
# Their symbols are USERSPACE_<NAME> like every ring-3 image (mk/vars.mk reads
# them to choose what the system volume carries), but these programs are not
# directories under userspace/, so config/Kconfig.userspace (generated from
# those) does not declare them.

config USERSPACE_RG
    bool "RG.ELF: ripgrep 15.2.0 (third_party/ports/ripgrep)"
    depends on !HWCLASS_EMBEDDED
    default y if PRESET_DESKTOP || PRESET_SERVER
    default n
    help
      ripgrep, a recursive line-oriented search (`rg PATTERN [PATH]`), ported to
      the native SDK std target: a std program on the vendored crates, with no C
      (no PCRE2). It reads files and directories beneath the read-only root
      directory its topology row grants (std::fs over the `*at` node ops), writes
      to the console or a redirected stdout, and holds nothing else. Unlicense OR
      MIT. Built by `make ports`.

      y: the system volume carries /fat/RG.ELF and the built-in topology has its
      row (the shell may start it). Cost: the image's size on the volume
      (3.3 to 3.8 MB, by ISA).

config USERSPACE_FD
    bool "FD.ELF: fd 10.5.2 (third_party/ports/fd-find)"
    depends on !HWCLASS_EMBEDDED
    default y if PRESET_DESKTOP || PRESET_SERVER
    default n
    help
      fd, a file finder (`fd PATTERN [PATH]`), ported to the native SDK std
      target without its signal handler, owner filter and device-type probes
      (which need unix). It lists directories beneath the read-only root
      directory its topology row grants and writes to the console or a
      redirected stdout. MIT OR Apache-2.0. Built by `make ports`.

      y: the system volume carries /fat/FD.ELF and the built-in topology has its
      row (the shell may start it). Cost: the image's size on the volume
      (2.4 to 2.9 MB, by ISA).
